            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a footpath, then the Telugu for to break a rule."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: దిశ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దిశ — diśa — \"a compass direction; a side\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సూర్యుడు తూర్పు దిశలో ఉదయిస్తాడు. sūryuḍu tūrpu diśalō udayistāḍu. The sun rises in the east."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The four directions are తూర్పు, పడమర, ఉత్తరం and దక్షిణం. దిక్కు is a more everyday word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దిశ (diśa) is borrowed from Sanskrit diśā, \"direction, region\" (CDIAL 6339)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
