          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సూచిక — sūcika — \"a signpost; an indicator\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ సూచిక మీద నగరానికి దూరం రాసి ఉంది. ā sūcika mīda nagarāniki dūraṁ rāsi undi. The distance to the city is written on that signpost."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Any sign that tells you something: a signpost, an index in a book, a gauge on a dashboard."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సూచిక (sūcika) is built from Sanskrit sūc, \"to indicate, to make known\", whose noun sūcaka means \"one that indicates\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
